essories, electronics, and jewelry products through its websites, other interactive media, and catalogs, as well as operates as an online retailer. The company operates multiple platforms, including broadcast networks, websites, mobile applications, social media pages, print catalogs, and physical stores. The company was formerly known as Qurate Retail, Inc. and changed its name to QVC Group, Inc. in February 2025. QVC Group, Inc. was founded in 1991 and is based in West Chester, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael A. George | Chair of the Board & Interim CEO | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $491K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $888 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["QVC Group, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $399M market cap on $8.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -3.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $287M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.2pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 50% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5019715782865947},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 32% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 86/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 111% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (82% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $5.3M) \